   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y8r1-do-now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Key Words (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why do we need both INPUT and OUTPUT?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>INPUT brings a value in from the user. OUTPUT shows the answer back to them.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From Lesson 1.</p><div id=\"y8r1-do-now\"></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Which symbol stores a value in a variable?",
     "options": [
      "=",
      "<-",
      "+",
      ">"
     ],
     "correct": 1,
     "explain": "The arrow <- stores the value on its right in the variable on its left."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "Which keyword takes a value typed in by the user?",
     "options": [
      "OUTPUT",
      "DECLARE",
      "INPUT"
     ],
     "correct": 2,
     "explain": "INPUT takes a value from the user."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Trace (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y8r1-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y8r1_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Trace (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why is the output not 4?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Line 3 changes Number before line 4 outputs it. The lines run in order.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">From Lesson 1. Trace the program.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Number : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;Number &lt;- 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;Number &lt;- Number + 3</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Number</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-do-now-2-a\">(a) What is the value of Number after line 2? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Trace (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-do-now-2-b\">(b) What is output? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Trace (2 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y8r1-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y8r1-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "title",
   "label": "Revision 1: Reading Pseudocode",
   "content": "<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Algorithms</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Revision 1: Reading Pseudocode</h2><p>Year 8</p></div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>Today:</strong> read a program and say what it outputs.</li><li><strong>Three ideas:</strong> sequence, selection, loops. Then flowcharts.</li><li><strong>Next lesson:</strong> arrays and searching. <strong>Then:</strong> the assessment.</li></ul><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why do programmers write pseudocode before real code?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>It is easy to read and check. You can plan the steps without worrying about a real language.</p></div></details>"
  },
  {
   "id": "key-words",
   "label": "Key Words",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Key Words</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Which of these key words come in pairs? Why?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>IF goes with ENDIF. FOR goes with NEXT. The second word shows where the block <strong>ends</strong>.</p></div></details><table class=\"donow-table\" style=\"font-size:17px;width:100%\"><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">DECLARE Age : INTEGER</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">make a variable (a name for a value)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">Age &lt;- 12</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">store a value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">INPUT Age</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">take a value from the user</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">OUTPUT Age</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">show a value</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">IF ... THEN ... ELSE ... ENDIF</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">choose what to do (<strong>selection</strong>)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-family:monospace\">FOR ... NEXT</td><td style=\"padding:7px 12px;text-align:left\">repeat lines (<strong>a loop</strong>)</td></tr></table>"
  },
  {
   "id": "sequence",
   "label": "Sequence: One Line at a Time",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Sequence: One Line at a Time</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: the user types 12. What is output? Why?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Output: <strong>13</strong>.</p><p>Line 2 stores 12 in Age. Line 3 adds 1. Line 4 shows Age. The lines run <strong>in order</strong>, one at a time: this is <strong>sequence</strong>.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Age : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Age</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;Age &lt;- Age + 1</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT Age</div></div></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>The computer runs <strong>line 1</strong>, then <strong>line 2</strong>, then <strong>line 3</strong>.</li><li>Write down the value after each line.</li><li>A new value <strong>replaces</strong> the old one.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "sequence-check",
   "label": "Check: Sequence",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y8r1-sequence-check",
   "validatorKey": "y8r1_sequence_check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Sequence</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does B stay 2?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>No line after line 4 stores a new value in B.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE A : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE B : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;A &lt;- 5</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;B &lt;- 2</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;A &lt;- A + B</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT A</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-sequence-check-a\">(a) What is the value of A after line 5? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-sequence-check-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"sequence-check-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Sequence part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-sequence-check-b\">(b) What is the value of B at the end? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-sequence-check-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"sequence-check-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Sequence part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y8r1-sequence-check-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y8r1-sequence-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "selection",
   "label": "Selection: Choosing a Path",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Selection: Choosing a Path</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: the user types 70. Then 30. What is output each time? Why only one OUTPUT?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>70: 70 &gt;= 50 is TRUE, so <strong>Pass</strong>. 30: FALSE, so <strong>Fail</strong>.</p><p>IF chooses <strong>one</strong> path. TRUE runs the THEN line. FALSE runs the ELSE line.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Mark : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Mark</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Mark &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">7&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div></div></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><code>&gt;=</code> means <strong>more than or equal to</strong>.</li><li><code>&gt;</code> means <strong>more than</strong>.</li><li>TRUE: the line after <strong>THEN</strong> runs.</li><li>FALSE: the line after <strong>ELSE</strong> runs.</li><li><strong>ENDIF</strong> ends the choice.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "compare",
   "label": "Compare: >= and >",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Compare: &gt;= and &gt;</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">The user types 50 into both. What does each one output? Why are they different?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>A outputs <strong>Pass</strong>: 50 &gt;= 50 is TRUE.</p><p>B outputs <strong>Fail</strong>: 50 &gt; 50 is FALSE. 50 is not more than 50.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">Program A</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">INPUT Mark</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF Mark &gt;= 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div></div><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px;font-weight:700;text-align:center\">Program B</p><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">INPUT Mark</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">IF Mark &gt; 50 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">ENDIF</div></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "selection-check",
   "label": "Check: Selection",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y8r1-selection-check",
   "validatorKey": "y8r1_selection_check",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check: Selection</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does 25 give Cold?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>25 is not more than 25, so Temp > 25 is FALSE.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Temp : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Temp</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Temp &gt; 25 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Hot\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Cold\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">7&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-selection-check-a\">(a) The user types 30. What is output? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-selection-check-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"selection-check-a\" aria-label=\"Check: Selection part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-selection-check-b\">(b) The user types 25. What is output? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-selection-check-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"selection-check-b\" aria-label=\"Check: Selection part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y8r1-selection-check-c\">(c) The user types 25. Which line number runs: 5 or 7? [1]</label><input id=\"y8r1-selection-check-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"selection-check-c\" aria-label=\"Check: Selection part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y8r1-selection-check-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y8r1-selection-check-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop",
   "label": "Loops: Repeating Lines",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Loops: Repeating Lines</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Predict: how many times is Hi output? Why use a loop, and not write OUTPUT four times?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the worked answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Count goes 1, 2, 3, 4, so Hi is output <strong>4 times</strong>.</p><p>A loop is shorter. To output it 100 times, you only change 4 to 100.</p></div></details><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;DECLARE Count : INTEGER</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 4</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Hi\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;NEXT Count</div></div></div><div><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li><strong>FOR Count &lt;- 1 TO 4</strong>: Count starts at 1 and goes up to 4.</li><li>The lines between FOR and NEXT run <strong>once for each value</strong>.</li><li><strong>NEXT</strong> adds 1 to Count and goes back to the top.</li></ul></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "activity-1",
   "label": "Activity 1: Trace a Loop",
   "type": "embedded-app",
